My Jupyter Book Project

This is a starter template for building a website from Jupyter Notebooks, complete with LaTeX/BibTeX support and PDF output, deployed automatically using GitHub Actions.

This project is built using Jupyter Book.

Project Structure

.
├── .github/workflows/deploy.yml  # GitHub Action for auto-deployment
├── content/                     # Your book's content
│   ├── _bibliography.bib        # Your BibTeX citation file
│   └── notebook1.ipynb          # A sample notebook
├── _config.yml                  # Main configuration file
├── _toc.yml                     # Table of Contents (site navigation)
├── README.md                    # This file
└── requirements.txt             # Python dependencies


How to Use This Template

1. Local Setup (Optional, but Recommended)

You can build and preview the website on your local machine before pushing it to GitHub.

Prerequisites:

Python 3.8+

A LaTeX distribution (like TeX Live or MiKTeX) is required only if you want to build PDFs locally.

Installation:

Create and activate a virtual environment (recommended):

python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate  # On Windows, use `.venv\Scripts\activate`


Install the required packages:

pip install -r requirements.txt


2. Add Your Content

Add Notebooks/Markdown: Place your .ipynb and .md files inside the content/ directory.

Update Table of Contents: Edit _toc.yml to reflect your site's structure.

Add Citations: Add your BibTeX entries to content/_bibliography.bib.

Cite in Notebooks: In any Markdown cell, you can use:

LaTeX equations: $E = mc^2$ (inline) or $$...$$ (display).

Citations: {cite}`einstein1905` (or whatever your BibTeX key is).

3. Build Your Book Locally

Build the HTML Website:

Run this command from the project's root directory:

jupyter-book build .


The website will be generated in the _build/html/ directory. You can open the _build/html/index.html file in your browser to see it.

Build the PDF Manuscript:

Ensure you have a full LaTeX distribution installed.

jupyter-book build . --builder pdflatex


The PDF will be generated in the _build/latex/ directory (e.g., book.pdf).

4. GitHub Deployment (Automatic)

This template is configured to build and deploy your website automatically using GitHub Actions and GitHub Pages.

Setup Steps:

Create a GitHub Repository: Create a new repository on GitHub and push these files to it (on the main branch).

Enable GitHub Pages:

Go to your repository's Settings tab.

In the left sidebar, click on Pages.

Under "Build and deployment", set the Source to GitHub Actions.

That's it! Now, every time you push a change to your main branch, the GitHub Action defined in .github/workflows/deploy.yml will automatically:

Check out your code.

Install the Python dependencies.

Build the HTML version of your Jupyter Book.

Push the built website to a special branch called gh-pages.

GitHub Pages will serve your site from that gh-pages branch.

Your website will be available at https://ucf-photovoltaics.github.io/photovoltaics-knowledge-base/.
